OR 1.64 (95% CI 1.5-1.8) p ≤0.001. Medium social support OR 1.32 (95% CI 1.2-1.44) p ≤0.001 (Table 5).\n\nLoneliness\n\nThe mean loneliness score was 'not lonely' and ranged from 4.67 (SE 0.021) in week 1, with a slight increase in\n\nloneliness (shown by an increase in mean score) to 4.8 (SE 0.023) in week 8. The percentage of people who reported as lonely, per the UCLA scale, was 31.5% in week 1, increasing to 35.5% in week 8; a chi squared test showed no statistical difference in loneliness between week 1 and week 8. There was a reduction in likelihood of being active amongst people who were lonely when accounting for sex and age, OR 0.92 (95% CI 0.86-0.98) p =0.011 although the association was attenuated after further covariate adjustments (Table 5).\n\n1 Springer", "width": 1654, "height": 2197, "blocks": [{"kind": "text", "text": "Table 1 Baseline characteristics of participants (n = 16,980)", "bbox": {"x": 134.1, "y": 156.5, "width": 316.1, "height": 60.60000000000002}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Variable", "bbox": {"x": 491.7, "y": 162.9, "width": 89.40000000000003, "height": 35.099999999999994}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Gender Female Male Age category 18-29 30-45 46-59 60+ Ethnicity White BAME Income > £30 K/year < £30 K/year Education", "bbox": {"x": 482.9, "y": 292.6, "width": 146.30000000000007, "height": 509.0}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "2 degree Shigh school Employed Yes Key worker Yes Carer Yes Lives alone", "bbox": {"x": 488.4, "y": 817.1, "width": 143.89999999999998, "height": 297.4}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Yes Urban living Yes Chronic health condition Yes Physical health condition Yes", "bbox": {"x": 491.7, "y": 1130.4, "width": 258.59999999999997, "height": 226.79999999999995}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Mental health condition Yes Active prior to lockdown Yes", "bbox": {"x": 491.7, "y": 1373.1, "width": 255.8, "height": 124.60000000000014}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "Total sample (n = 16,980)", "bbox": {"x": 788.7, "y": 172.3, "width": 131