ere was a reduction in likelihood of being active amongst people who were lonely when accounting for sex and age, OR 0.92 (95% CI 0.86-0.98) p =0.011 although the association was attenuated after further covariate adjustments (Table 5).", "bbox": {"x": 846.0, "y": 1593.3, "width": 667.5999999999999, "height": 335.79999999999995}}, {"kind": "text", "text": "1 Springer", "bbox": {"x": 136.3, "y": 2045.8, "width": 126.5, "height": 37.700000000000045}}], "ms": 273.27}